<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p>
    <h2>Nobody ever taught you what happens after you talk.</h2>
    <p>Not in school. Not in onboarding. Not in the feedback you've gotten since — because the one thing you most need feedback on, whether you actually landed, is the one thing almost nobody will tell you directly.</p>
    <p>So you've been paying a tax you can't see. The promotion that went to someone who explained their work more simply. The meeting where you said the smart thing first and someone else got the credit ten minutes later. Nobody sends you an invoice for it.</p>
    <p>This is where you learn to read the invoice — and stop paying it.</p>
    <div class="pull">
      <p>Free, no signup, no exam at the end. <strong>The only test that matters is your next real conversation.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How this works</p>
    <h2>Short chapters. Real moments. One thing to notice.</h2>
    <p>Every chapter is five to ten minutes — built to be read between meetings, not studied like a textbook.</p>
    <p>Each one opens with a moment you'll recognize. That's on purpose. You don't learn a habit by being told to have it — you learn it by seeing where the old one was costing you.</p>
    <p>Every module ends with a <strong>Notice This</strong> prompt. Not a quiz. One thing to watch for in your next real conversation. Notice, adjust, notice again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

